messages.content:
This screen belongs to a clickable mockup of: A tiny bakery website

Show this screen: Cart screen of a bakery website with one sourdough loaf added

Screens of this mockup, as a tree:
@home: the first screen of A tiny bakery website
  @sourdough-details: Details of a sourdough loaf at a bakery website, with price and add-to-cart
  @almond-croissant-details: Details of an almond croissant at a bakery website, with price and add-to-cart
  @cart: Cart screen of a bakery website with one sourdough loaf added (this screen)
    @checkout: The checkout screen (not made yet)
      @order-confirmation: The order confirmation screen (not made yet)
  @menu: Menu screen of a tiny bakery website listing breads, pastries and cakes (not made yet)
  @cinnamon-roll-details: Details of a cinnamon roll at a bakery website, with price and add-to-cart (not made yet)

The spec of this mockup: decisions every screen follows, one per line; a row with ? is not decided yet.
product.core-flow = @home → @menu → @cart → @checkout → @order-confirmation
ui.nav = Tabs: Home @home, Menu @menu, Cart @cart
ui.back = ‹ Back, first in the header
ui.forms = Labels above inputs, errors in red text under the field, primary button full width in dark ink
ui.lists = Item name left, price right with two decimals, quantity as a stepper
ui.colors = Primary actions dark ink; errors red text; unavailable items grey with strikethrough
data.pricing = Prices in USD, tax included, shown with two decimals
data.fulfillment ? whether orders are for pickup, delivery, or both

Tabs of ui.nav: last on every screen, in this markup, one link per tab with its label and @name, and aria-current="page" on this screen's own tab: <nav data-ui="tabs"><a data-action="@name">Label</a>…</nav>. A ui.nav line names each tab by its label and @name, e.g. ui.nav = Tabs: Menu @home, Orders @order-list, Profile @profile
Back of ui.back: where ui.back says, with its label, in this markup: <a data-ui="back" data-action="back">Label</a>. The tab screens have no Back. A ui.back line starts with the label, e.g. ui.back = ‹ Back, first in the header

Design it for a phone screen, 390 px wide.

